# Urkaaaz — compact Tutorial Hint redesign

## Purpose

Create one high-fidelity visual concept for a smaller, more polished
`Tutorial Hint` card shown over the Urkaaaz match screen. This is a visual
redesign study only. Preserve tutorial behavior, target geometry, localization,
and game content; do not implement or invent new mechanics.

## Reference inputs

- Attach a screenshot of the current campaign match with a Tutorial Hint
  visible. Treat it as the source of truth for the screen composition, game
  art, tutorial target, and spotlight.
- Use the Shop, Dashboard, and Loadout screenshots only as references for the
  shared Urkaaaz visual language: painterly fantasy scenery, dark translucent
  panels, carved timber and iron, restrained warm-gold trim, and pale
  readable text.
- Redesign only the Tutorial Hint card and its controls. Keep the match
  background, HUD, target, and spotlight visually unchanged.
- Do not use any reference screenshot as a flattened background. Recreate
  the screen concept with visually separable game scenery, HUD, spotlight,
  hint panel, text, and controls.

## Output

- Generate exactly one PNG: `tutorial_hint_compact_concept_01.png`.
- Save it under `assets_src/tutorial/screen-concepts/`.
- Canvas: exactly 1920 × 1080 pixels, landscape 16:9.
- Show the complete match screen edge-to-edge, without a phone frame,
  presentation board, annotations, watermark, signature, or alternate
  concepts.
- This is a visual concept for review, not a production asset or replacement
  screen background. Keep the hint panel, text, and buttons visually
  separable for native Android recreation.

## Hint content

Use the following existing Polish tutorial copy exactly; do not rewrite,
paraphrase, truncate, or add instructional text:

- Title: `SAMOUCZEK`
- Message: `Zniszcz fortecę przeciwnika, aby wygrać. Zmniejsz jej zdrowie do zera, jednocześnie broniąc własnej.`
- Progress: `KROK 1 / 8`
- Secondary action: `POMIŃ`
- Primary action: `DALEJ`

Render all Polish characters correctly. Keep title, message, progress, and
actions as crisp live-looking interface text, not pseudo-text or decorative
lettering.

## Compact layout direction

- Make the card visibly smaller and shorter than in the reference screenshot:
  aim for roughly 270–280 dp maximum width and a compact height around
  190–240 dp for this example. Preserve comfortable safe margins.
- Keep the Hint beside the highlighted fortress, on the side with available
  space, with a visibly clear gap of at least 24 dp. Never overlap the target,
  crowd it, cover its spotlight opening, or obscure critical HUD controls.
- Center the card within that available dimmed region instead of aligning its
  edge directly beside the target. Balance the remaining space between the
  card, target, and screen edge.
- Consolidate the title and step progress into one compact header row:
  small gold `SAMOUCZEK` label on the left and discreet `KROK 1 / 8`
  progress on the right.
- Use a concise message area with balanced line breaks and clear line
  spacing. Keep the sample text intact and readable; reduce wasted padding
  before reducing text size. Supporting text should remain comfortably
  legible at normal mobile viewing scale.
- Place actions in one compact footer. Make `DALEJ` the clear but restrained
  gold primary button and `POMIŃ` a quieter dark or outlined secondary
  control. Keep both controls visually distinct and large enough for
  comfortable touch use; do not render oversized pale slabs.
- Use a compact dark charcoal/iron card with a thin bronze or warm-gold edge,
  a subtle inner bevel, and a soft shadow. Add only restrained corner details
  or small runic accents; keep the central text area uncluttered.
- Reuse the existing Urkaaaz UI frame and button art. Use the thin,
  rounded `match_hud_universal_frame` for the card,
  `ui_button_dark_xs_short` for `POMIŃ` and
  `loadout_start_match_button_xs_short` for `DALEJ`; do not invent new button
  artwork.
- Match the game's Cinzel SemiBold-style heading and button typography, with
  clean high-contrast body text. Use the established warm-gold, ivory, and
  charcoal palette.
- Make the result feel elegant, friendly, and game-native rather than like a
  generic Android dialog, a parchment popup, or an ornate quest scroll.

## Responsive and state requirements

- The card is a reusable Tutorial Hint component, not a one-off level popup.
  Keep the design viable for different localized message lengths and for
  steps with no target.
- The optional wind-strength legend must be able to fit as a small,
  secondary horizontal row without forcing the panel back to its current
  oversized height. Use only the three existing Low/Medium/High wind icons
  when the reference provides them; do not invent a fourth category or new
  gameplay icon.
- The Hint must continue to read as a separate layer from the dimmed match
  screen and soft-edged spotlight. Do not change the spotlight gradient or
  the exact highlighted target.
- Do not invent progress counts, rewards, mechanics, tutorial text, or
  additional controls.

## Negative requirements

- No full-screen tutorial dialog or giant panel.
- No oversized title, excessive padding, oversized buttons, or bright flat
  white button slabs.
- No new gameplay instructions, altered localization, extra tutorial steps,
  new mechanics, or invented status indicators.
- No arrows or pointers that touch or cover the spotlight target.
- No change to the match HUD, battlefield, fortress, camera, target bounds,
  spotlight opening, or spotlight gradient.
- No new characters, scenery, maps, reward icons, ad controls, or unrelated
  navigation.
- No flattened production background, device frame, watermark, signature,
  illegible pseudo-text, or cropped controls.

## Review checklist

- Confirm the hint is clearly smaller and shorter than the reference.
- Confirm every sample string is exact, readable, and correctly accented.
- Confirm the target and its spotlight remain unobstructed.
- Confirm `DALEJ` is the primary action and `POMIŃ` remains available as a
  quieter secondary action.
- Confirm the card remains legible and visually coherent with the existing
  Urkaaaz HUD at landscape mobile scale.
- Confirm all visible screen elements remain separable for native UI
  recreation.
